; FILED: `tensor?` disagrees on a reader literal.
; native -r : #t  #t   (a numeric #(...) literal IS a tensor natively)
; vm        : #f  #t   (the VM compiles #(...) to a vector value)
;
; Every SIZE and RANK property of literals is identical across substrates (see
; corpus/37_tensor_literal_generality.esk); this is purely which predicate the
; literal's runtime representation answers, i.e. operand classification.
(display (tensor? #(1 2 3))) (newline)
(display (vector? #(1 2 3))) (newline)
